  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 224 PM EDT Thu Sep 17 2026\nHigh pressure continues aloft over the southeast this afternoon with \na low just east of Florida. At the surface, the Atlantic ridge axis \nextends north of the state, keeping an easterly boundary layer flow \nin place. A few showers have continued to push onshore from the \nAtlantic and this trend will continue through the rest of the day, \nwith relatively drier air limiting overall coverage. \n\nFor Friday through the weekend, the surface high will shift \nsouthward as the mid/upper-level low moves westward across the state \nand then over the Gulf. Moisture will go back up during this period \nand this combined with the low aloft will lead to increased shower \nand storm chances, generally moving from the coast toward the \ninterior in continued onshore flow. Then for early to mid next week, \nwinds remain rather light and mostly onshore, with abundant moisture \ncontinuing to allow scattered to numerous storms each afternoon and \nevening as the sea breeze develops and shifts inland.",
